# CrowPanel ESP32 4.2" e-Paper HMI Display — Technical Specifications

Resolution: 400 × 300 pixels (black and white).
Manufacturer: Elecrow.
Verified: 2026-10-27.

## Hardware

| Parameter | Specification |
| --- | --- |
| Screen diagonal | 4.2 inches |
| Technology | Active Matrix Electrophoretic Display (AM EPD) |
| Display controller | SSD1683 |
| MCU module | ESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N8R8 |
| CPU frequency | Up to 240 MHz |
| Flash / PSRAM | 8 MB / 8 MB |
| Active display area | 84.8 × 63.6 mm |
| Pixel pitch | 0.212 × 0.212 mm |
| Viewing angle | Full viewing angle |
| Display interface | 3-wire / 4-wire SPI |
| Refresh support | Partial refresh |
| Connections | UART0 ×1, BAT ×1, GPIO connector ×1, TF (microSD) slot ×1 |
| Controls | Rotary switch, Menu, Exit, Reset, Boot |
| Development environments | Arduino IDE, ESP-IDF, MicroPython |
| Display operating voltage | 2.2–3.7 V |
| Operating temperature | 0–50 °C |
| Storage temperature | −25–70 °C |

The display is reflective, requires ambient light rather than a backlight,
and retains its image when power is removed.

## Display GPIO mapping

| Signal | ESP32-S3 GPIO |
| --- | --- |
| SCK | 12 |
| MOSI | 11 |
| RES (reset) | 47 |
| DC (data/command) | 46 |
| CS (chip select) | 45 |
| BUSY | 48 |

## Integration notes

- The voltage range above is explicitly labeled as the display operating
  voltage in Elecrow's repository. It must not be treated as a specification
  for every board power input or GPIO.
- A packed 1-bit 400 × 300 framebuffer requires 15,000 bytes (calculated:
  400 × 300 ÷ 8), excluding library overhead and additional buffers.
- Refresh duration and board sleep current depend on firmware and hardware;
  no guaranteed values are specified here.

